     8│ //
     9│ // Root-cause closure: given a list of Violations from one contract
    10│ // check, group them by (kind, fingerprint) and use ViolKindSpec.Implies
    11│ // to mark symptom violations as derived. The retry hint builder
    12│ // then surfaces only the root violation per group, eliminating the
    13│ // "fix one, three new ones appear" rotation pattern observed in
    14│ // qfa-mr3 (docs/design/iteration_inflation_remediation.md §3 Source #1).
    15│ //
    16│ // Algorithm (per fingerprint group):
    17│ //   1. Walk Implies graph forward — A.Implies = [B] means "if A and
    18│ //      B fire on the same fingerprint, B is a symptom of A".
    19│ //   2. Within a fingerprint group, prefer kinds that imply others
